# Python
.venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info
build/
dist/

# uv.lock IS committed as of 2026-09-10. The comment that used to sit here
# argued the opposite, and its reasoning was right at the time: nothing read
# or enforced the lock, so a committed one would be an unmaintained, silently
# stale duplicate. The fix was to make it enforced rather than to keep it out
# — `uv sync --locked` is now the documented install path in the Makefile AND
# the `core`/`perf-timing` CI jobs, and `--locked` FAILS rather than silently
# re-resolving when the lock and pyproject disagree.
#
# Do NOT re-ignore it without also removing those, or the two halves go back
# to describing different environments — which is the whole class of bug this
# change exists to close (three of them, 09-07 → 09-10).

